<%#
  The disclosure caret. Drawn rather than typed, like the thumbtack in
  `notes/_pin_icon`: the arrow glyphs (▸ ▾) differ in weight and in vertical
  centring between macOS and Android, and this tree is meant to survive being
  translated into an Android theme (PRD §13).

  One drawing, rotated by CSS off `aria-expanded`, rather than two: a caret
  that turns reads as the same object moving, where swapping glyphs reads as
  two objects alternating.
%>
<svg class="caret-icon" width="9" height="9" viewBox="0 0 9 9" fill="none"
     aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path d="M2.5 1.25 L6.25 4.5 L2.5 7.75" stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
</svg>
